###Why is the stack approach optimal?
1. Single traversal: Each input character is processed once.
2. Efficient removal: pop_back() removes the last character without shifting all remaining characters.
3. Automatic cascading: If removing a pair makes two equal characters adjacent, the stack catches that when the next character is processed.
4. Linear time: Each character is pushed at most once and popped at most once, giving O(n) total time.
5. Best practical choice: It is simple, efficient, and works well for the maximum constraint n = 10^5.
The O(n) time complexity is asymptotically optimal because, in the general case, every input character must be examined.
